.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ag-doctor 1  "doctor 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
ag\-doctor \- Check the installation, the repository, your identity and every remote\*(Aqs credential
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag doctor\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check the installation, the repository, your identity and every remote\*(Aqs credential
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Do not contact any server: check that credentials exist, not that they work
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Exit with 1 when a check warns, not only when one fails
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR [default: 10]
How long to wait for each server before giving up
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
